    <p style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 24px;">
      A well-organized kitchen makes everyday cooking easier. Whether you live in a condominium, apartment, or landed house in Malaysia, the right cabinet arrangement can help you save space, find things quickly, and reduce clutter.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 36px;">
      You do not always need a larger kitchen. Sometimes, a better storage system makes the biggest difference.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 30px); color: var(--walnut); margin: 36px 0 16px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(61,43,31,0.08); pt-24; padding-top: 24px;">
      1. Start by Decluttering
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Before organizing your cabinets, remove everything and check what you actually use.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Group your kitchen items into categories such as plates, glasses, cookware, food containers, spices, and cleaning supplies.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 32px;">
      Keep frequently used items within easy reach. Donate or discard unnecessary items, and avoid storing damaged containers or utensils you no longer need.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 30px); color: var(--walnut); margin: 36px 0 16px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(61,43,31,0.08); padding-top: 24px;">
      2. Organize Cabinets by Daily Use
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Place everyday plates, bowls, and glasses close to the areas where you use them.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Store heavy pots and pans in lower cabinets whenever possible. Reserve higher shelves for lighter items that you use less frequently.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 32px;">
      This arrangement makes your kitchen more convenient and helps you avoid repeatedly reaching for heavy cookware.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 30px); color: var(--walnut); margin: 36px 0 16px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(61,43,31,0.08); padding-top: 24px;">
      3. Use Pull-Out Drawers and Organizers
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Deep cabinets can become difficult to manage because items at the back are hard to reach.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Pull-out drawers, adjustable dividers, and internal cabinet organizers can make better use of available storage space.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Consider dedicated compartments for cutlery, cooking utensils, lids, and spices.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 32px;">
      You can also use simple organizers inside existing cabinets without replacing the entire kitchen.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 30px); color: var(--walnut); margin: 36px 0 16px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(61,43,31,0.08); padding-top: 24px;">
      4. Make Better Use of Vertical Space
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      If your cabinets have tall shelves, consider using stackable organizers or adjustable shelving.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      These solutions can create more usable space while keeping your items visible.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 32px;">
      However, avoid overloading shelves. Always consider the cabinet material, shelf support, and weight of the items being stored.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 30px); color: var(--walnut); margin: 36px 0 16px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(61,43,31,0.08); padding-top: 24px;">
      5. Consider Malaysia's Humid Climate
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Kitchen cabinets can be exposed to moisture from cooking, cleaning, and nearby sinks.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      Wipe up spills promptly, repair leaks, and avoid putting wet items into enclosed cabinets.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 32px;">
      When choosing new cabinets, discuss suitable materials and finishes with your cabinet supplier, particularly for areas around the sink.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 30px); color: var(--walnut); margin: 36px 0 16px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(61,43,31,0.08); padding-top: 24px;">
      6. Plan Storage Before Ordering New Cabinets
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 20px;">
      If you are considering a kitchen renovation, list your storage needs before finalizing the cabinet design.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-body); margin-bottom: 12px;">
      Think about:
    </p>
    <ul style="margin-bottom: 24px; padding-left: 24px; color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.8;">
      <li>How often you cook</li>
      <li>The amount of cookware you own</li>
      <li>Where appliances will be placed</li>
      <li>Whether you need deep drawers or open shelves</li>
      <li>The available kitchen measurements</li>
      <li>Your preferred cabinet materials and budget</li>
    </ul>
